Z||000008||00lE||06-27-2001||05:11 PM||||When a person sells a product via the internet, and they know that the product is not as implied (ie. will not work as intended) they are guilty of felony mail/wire fraud.  Plain as that.  Ebay has a very nice system to deal with this type of abuse.  There is a fraud report form located at the Safe Harbor section that should be filled out promptly.  I know as a fact that eBay does prosecute offenders on large ticket items or multiple violations, and they will pull the account on those suspected of any fraudulent activity.  Every ebay transaction is also insured for amounts over $25 (there is a $25 deductable) by Loyds of London.  Most of these ripoffs count on the fact that the buyers do not know about these protections..||||reg||1
